<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.13.2: Creating Exponential Functions from Graphs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01481</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.13.2: Creating Exponential Functions from Graphs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>46990163-00b1-4989-bb07-4275aa15a88a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Examine the graph representing an exponential function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. The function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> gives the value of a computer, in
  dollars, as a function of time, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, measured in years since the time of purchase.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
        
          <media alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL DECAY FUNCTION, WHERE VALUE IN DOLLARS IS A FUNCTION OF TIME. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS 0 COMMA FOUR HUNDRED, 2 COMMA 100, AND 4 COMMA 25.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_03_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00003">Based on the graph, what can you say about the following?</para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004"> The purchase price of the computer</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005"/>
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00007">$400</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 1</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00009"/>
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00011"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>200</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      
        <exercise id="exer-00003">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00012"> The meaning of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00013">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00015">The value of the computer after 1 year</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00004">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00016"> How the value of the computer is changing each year</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00018">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00019">The computer loses half of its value each year.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00005">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00020">An equation that defines <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. (If needed, use the '^' symbol to enter an exponent.)</para>
            <para id="para-00021">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00023"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>400</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> or equivalent (i.e., <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>400</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00006">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00024">Whether the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> will reach 0 after 10 years</para>
            <para id="para-00025">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00026">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00027">No, it will not. After 10 years, the value of the computer will be a little less than $0.40.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      <para id="para-00028">For questions 7 - 10, examine the graphs of the exponential functions.</para>
      <para id="para-00029">Examine the graph of the exponential function below.<media alt="">
  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_03_02.jpg"/></media></para>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00007">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00030"> Write an equation that defines the function. Use the “^” symbol to enter an exponent.</para>
            <para id="para-00031">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00032">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00033"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00008">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00034">For each, write an equation that defines the function and find the value of the function when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 5.</para>
            <para id="para-00035">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00036">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00037"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>215</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      <para id="para-00038">Examine the graph of the exponential function below. <media alt=""><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_03_03.jpg"/></media></para>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00009">
          <problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00039"> Write an equation that defines the function. Use the “^” symbol to enter an exponent.</para><para id="para-00040">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00041">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00042"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> (or equivalent, i.e., <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00010">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00043">For each, write an equation that defines the function and find the value of the function when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 5.</para>
            <para id="para-00044">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00045">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00046"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0.625</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <section id="sect-00002">
      <title> Video: Interpreting an Exponential Function from a Graph</title>
      <para id="para-00047">Watch the following video to learn more about interpreting exponential functions:</para>
      <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
        <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/caccc8b7929b24bca06458ed8e8c609a93390e10"/>
      </media></section>
      <!-- "Start "Are you Ready for More? click to reveal.  If you have more than one on a page, you will need to change the Data-fire/data-wait-for-events for each set.-->
      
      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Are you ready for more?</title>
          <section id="sect-00004">
            <title>Extend Your Thinking</title>
      
      <!--Start interaction.  If multiple interactions appear under "are you ready for more?, they should all have matching "data-wait-for-event", which should also match the "data-fire-event" for the button. Note in this sample, they are all RFM1-->
      <exercise class="RFM1" id="exer-00011">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <title> Extending Your Thinking</title>
          <para id="para-00048">Consider a function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00049">If the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> goes through the points <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, would you expect <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> to be less
      than, equal to, or greater than 20?</para>
          <para id="para-00050">If the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> goes through the points <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, would you expect <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> to be less
      than, equal to, or greater than 20?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">
          <para id="para-00051"/>
          <para id="para-00052">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00053">The value 20 is what you would get for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> if <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> were a linear function through <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>
      (or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>). Looking at graphs representing our exponential functions, we can see that the line
      connecting two points on the graph always seems to be above the graph of the exponential function itself. Thus, we
      would expect <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in both cases.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--End interaction-->
    </section></section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <para id="para-00054">Which of the following is the function for the curve graphed below?</para>
      <para id="para-00055">
        
          <media alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS 0 COMMA 100, 1 COMMA THREE HUNDRED, AND 2 COMMA 900.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_04_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
    </note>
    <section id="sect-00005">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      
    <section id="sect-00006">
      <title> Writing Functions from Graphs</title>
      <para id="para-00056">
          <media alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS 0 COMMA 4, 1 COMMA 12, AND 2 COMMA 36.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_05_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00057">Find the equation of the function graphed above. Then find the value at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
                  <item>Find the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the starting point.</item>
                </list>
             </emphasis> 
            </entry>
            <entry>
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00002">
                  <item>Find the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the growth factor.</item>
                </list>
             </emphasis> 
            </entry>
            <entry>
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00003">
                  <item>Write the equation of the function.</item>
                </list>
             </emphasis> 
            </entry>
            <entry>
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00004">
                  <item>Find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
                </list>
             </emphasis> 
            </entry>
            <entry>
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>972</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
      </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
      <title> Try It: Writing Functions from Graphs</title>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00012">
          <problem id="prob-00012">
            <para id="para-00058">Use the graph below to write the equation of the function. Then find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00059">
                      <media alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS 0 COMMA 2, 1 COMMA 8, AND 2 COMMA 32.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_05_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00060">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00012">
            <para id="para-00061">Compare your answers:</para>
            <para id="para-00062">Here is how to write the exponential function from the graph:</para>
            <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00002">
              <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
                      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00005">
                        <item>Find the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the starting point.</item>
                      </list>
                   </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
        </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
                      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00006">
                        <item>Find the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the growth factor.</item>
                      </list>
                   </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
        </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
                      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00007">
                        <item>Write the equation of the function.</item>
                      </list>
                   </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>
        </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
                      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00008">
                        <item>Find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
                      </list>
                   </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2048</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
        </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </note>
    </section>
    </section>
    
  </content>
</document>
